<body>
    <h1>AI+ Installer Documentation</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <h2 id=3D"AI+InstallerDocumentation-Overview"><strong>Overview</str=
ong></h2>
<p>The AI+ Installer does the installation of AI+ services, including sytem=
 pre-checks, AWS configuration, and service integrations via a web-based UI=
.</p>
<p>This guide is going to help you in following the steps required to insta=
ll it on a fresh system.</p>
<hr>
<h2 id=3D"AI+InstallerDocumentation-1.Prerequisites"><strong>1. Prerequisit=
es</strong></h2>
<p>Before starting the installation:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Ensure GPU (Nvidia) drivers are correctly installed.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Copy the AI+ installation file to the <strong>home directory</strong> of=
 the user that will install the AI+ Admin Panel and run the AI+ services.</=
p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Syntax:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">scp &lt=
;path_to_installer_file&gt; &lt;remote_user&gt;@&lt;remote_host&gt;:&lt;tar=
get_directory&gt;</pre>
</div>
</div></li>
<li>
<p>For example:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">scp aip=
lus-installer-2025_07_23 aiplus-testing@10.161.0.72:~</pre>
</div>
</div></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>Make the installer file as an executable. For example:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">chmod +=
x aiplus-installer-2025_07_23</pre>
</div>
</div></li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h2 id=3D"AI+InstallerDocumentation-2.RunningtheInstaller"><strong>2. Runni=
ng the Installer</strong></h2>
<h3 id=3D"AI+InstallerDocumentation-Step1:LaunchInstaller"><strong>Step 1: =
Launch Installer</strong></h3>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Run the installer file. For example:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence"> ./aipl=
us-installer-2025_07_23)</pre>
</div>
</div></li>
<li>
<p>Open your browser and go to <code>http://hostIP:3000</code>.</p></li>
</ul>
<h3 id=3D"AI+InstallerDocumentation-Step2:AcceptLicenseAgreement"><strong>S=
tep 2: Accept License Agreement</strong></h3>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Click <strong>Next</strong>.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Read the <strong>End User License Agreement (EULA)</strong>.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Scroll to the bottom and click <strong>Agree &amp; Next</strong>.</p></l=
i>
</ul>
<h3 id=3D"AI+InstallerDocumentation-Step3:RequirementsCheck"><strong>Step 3=
: Requirements Check</strong></h3>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Review hardware and system requirements.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Click <strong>Next</strong>.</p></li>
</ul>
<h3 id=3D"AI+InstallerDocumentation-Step4:InstallationPrompt"><strong>Step =
4: Installation Prompt </strong></h3>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Give the password for the user (sudo access is required for installing s=
ome packages)</p></li>
<li>
<p>Click <strong>Install.</strong></p></li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h2 id=3D"AI+InstallerDocumentation-3.AWSConfiguration"><strong>3. AWS Conf=
iguration</strong></h2>
<p>The installer requires AWS credentials to fetch the images of the servic=
es from ECR:</p>
<h3 id=3D"AI+InstallerDocumentation-Step1:EnterCredentials"><strong>Step 1:=
 Enter Credentials</strong></h3>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>AWS Access Key ID</strong> =E2=86=92 Click <strong>Send</strong>=
</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>AWS Secret Access Key</strong> =E2=86=92 Click <strong>Send</str=
ong></p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Default Region</strong> (optional) =E2=86=92 Click <strong>Send<=
/strong></p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Default Output Format</strong> (optional) =E2=86=92 Click <stron=
g>Send</strong></p></li>
</ul>
<h3 id=3D"AI+InstallerDocumentation-Step2:ContinueInstallation"><strong>Ste=
p 2: Continue Installation</strong></h3>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Click <strong>Next</strong> to proceed.</p></li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h2 id=3D"AI+InstallerDocumentation-4.CompletingtheInstallation"><strong>4.=
 Completing the Installation</strong></h2>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Click <strong>Install</strong> to begin the installation.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Once finished, click the provided link to open the <strong>Admin UI</str=
ong>.</p></li>
<li>
<p>It should be at the <code>http://hostIP:8080</code> endpoint.</p></li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h2 id=3D"AI+InstallerDocumentation-5.EasySetupWizard(AdminUI)"><strong>5. =
Easy Setup Wizard (Admin UI)</strong></h2>
<h3 id=3D"AI+InstallerDocumentation-Step1:ServiceSelection"><strong>Step 1:=
 Service Selection</strong></h3>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Click <strong>Next</strong> on the welcome screen.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Select the services you want to install (e.g MetaGen).</p></li>
<li>
<p>Click <strong>Next</strong>.</p></li>
</ul>
<h3 id=3D"AI+InstallerDocumentation-Step2:IntegrationConfiguration"><strong=
>Step 2: Integration Configuration</strong></h3>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Choose the integrations you want to configure. (e.g Iris)</p></li>
<li>
<p>Click <strong>Next</strong>.</p></li>
</ul>
<h3 id=3D"AI+InstallerDocumentation-Step3:MountPathSetup"><strong>Step 3: M=
ount Path Setup</strong></h3>
<ul>
<li>
<p>For any selected integration, <strong>set the mount path as </strong><co=
de>/mmfs1/data</code>.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Click <strong>Next</strong>.</p></li>
</ul>
<h3 id=3D"AI+InstallerDocumentation-Step4:Confirmation"><strong>Step 4: Con=
firmation</strong></h3>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Review your selections.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Click <strong>Install</strong> to begin the final setup.</p></li>
</ul>
<blockquote>
<p>Note: Installation time may vary based on selected services and internet=
 connection.</p>
</blockquote>
<h3 id=3D"AI+InstallerDocumentation-Step5:Completion"><strong>Step 5: Compl=
etion</strong></h3>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Once installation completes, click <strong>Finish</strong>. You will be =
then redirected to the <strong>AI+ Admin UI.</strong></p></li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h2 id=3D"AI+InstallerDocumentation-6.Post-Installation"><strong>6. Post-In=
stallation</strong></h2>
<p>You can now access and manage AI+ services via the <strong>Admin UI</str=
ong>.</p>
<p>You can do things such as stop, start, restart them as well as view logs=
, check API docs for any selected service, pull various versions from ECR f=
or any of the services.</p>
<hr>
<h2 id=3D"AI+InstallerDocumentation-7.AdditionalReferences"><strong>7. Addi=
tional References</strong></h2>
<h4 id=3D"AI+InstallerDocumentation-Formorereference,downloadthedetailedins=
tallationguideinPDFformat:">For more reference, download the detailed insta=
llation guide in PDF format:</h4>
<p></p>
<p class=3D"media-group"><img height=3D"250" style=3D"margin: 2px; border: =
1px solid #ddd; box-sizing: border-box; vertical-align: text-bottom;" src=
=3D"ae35a9e333fa58e8197cdf5e17784d5965e1c750979495341cf63049dfc87f02" width=
=3D"250"></p>
<p></p>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
